#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter outlines the advanced features of &quantaplus; and how to use "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "&XML; Tools"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The 3.2 release of &quantaplus; brings with it many new &XML; tools and "
"features. The tools are unique in their integration within &quantaplus;. All "
"of these tools use <application>Kommander</application> as a front-end and "
"<application>libxml2</application> and <application>libxslt</application> as "
"a back-end. The combination of these makes for fast, efficient, productive, "
"and complete tools."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; Documentation Tools"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus; supports &kde;'s two main documentation tools: "
"<command>meinproc</command> and <command>checkXML</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: adv-quanta.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "meinproc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Anyone who has worked with &kde; documentation knows <command>meinproc</"
"command> and how superb it is. Well, take it up a notch with a great "
"graphical interface! No longer resort to a shell; just click the icon that "
"resembles a processor and you are done!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:60 adv-quanta.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current Working Folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This application expects an <filename>index.docbook</filename> file to be "
"present in a folder. If <filename>index.docbook</filename> is in the current "
"working folder, then simply leave <guilabel>Current Working Folder</"
"guilabel> checked. If it is not, then uncheck <guilabel>Current Working "
"Folder</guilabel> and enter the folder you wish to process in the "
"<guilabel>Other Folder</guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Outputted files are placed in the same folder as the sources files. All "
"&HTML; files are removed each time <command>meinproc</command> is ran."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: adv-quanta.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "checkXML"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again, anyone who has worked with &kde; documentation knows this helpful "
"application. Again, &quantaplus; provides a great little graphical front-end "
"to this one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the currently opened file is the <filename>index.docbook</filename> file, "
"then simply leave <guilabel>Current Working Folder</guilabel> checked. If it "
"is not, then uncheck <guilabel>Current Working Folder</guilabel> and enter "
"the folder of where <filename>index.docbook</filename> can be found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Output"
msgstr "Sortida"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is output, then your file is invalid. Please correct the reported "
"errors and try again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "&XML; Validation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus; has a great &XML; validation tool, which uses a "
"<command>xmllint</command> back-end."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:126 adv-quanta.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the file to be validated is currently focused on in &quantaplus;, then "
"simply leave <guilabel>Current File</guilabel> checked. If it is not, then "
"uncheck <guilabel>Current File</guilabel> and select the file to be "
"validated from the Other File file selector."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Well-formed Checking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only wish to know only if the file is well-formed, click the "
"<guilabel>Well-formed Checking Only</guilabel> check box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Definition &URI;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using a &DTD; and it is specified within the &XML; file, then "
"select &DTD; (Internal) (default), else select &DTD; (External) and locate "
"the &DTD; with the Definition &URI; file selector. Both &W3C; &XML; Schema "
"and RelaxNG validation are required to be externally defined via the "
"<guilabel>Definition &URI;</guilabel> file selector."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "&XSL; Processing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yep, &quantaplus; has a &XSL; processing tool, too! This uses the "
"<command>xsltproc</command> tool provided with <application>libxml2</"
"application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the file to be processed is currently focused on in &quantaplus;, then "
"simply leave <guilabel>Current File</guilabel> checked. If it is not, then "
"uncheck <guilabel>Current File</guilabel> and select the file to be "
"processed from the <guilabel>Other File</guilabel> selector."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: adv-quanta.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stylesheet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the &XSL; file that you wish to be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Output file name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the name of the file that you want the resulting file to be called. "
"File is outputed to your home folder by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "This application lacks flexibility. Sorry, we will do better next time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:295 adv-quanta.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: adv-quanta.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Mathieu</firstname> <surname>Kooiman</surname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: email
#: adv-quanta.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "quanta@map-is.nl"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is a Plugin?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus; is able to load plugins, which are KParts. The KPart framework "
"is another very powerfull framework of &kde;. A KPart is a relatively small, "
"reusable container of functionality. It allows &kde; developers to easily "
"build on the work of other programmers. One example of this is &quantaplus; "
"itself. The editor &quantaplus; uses is the &kate; KPart. The &kate; KPart "
"already had a bunch of functionality that &quantaplus; needed, like syntax "
"highlighting. Integrating it into &quantaplus; allowed the &quantaplus; "
"developers to focus on what &quantaplus; should be able to do, rather than "
"facing the many problems that developing a new editor KPart/component from "
"scratch would bring."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugins &quantaplus; loads might have nothing to do with &quantaplus; "
"itself. This makes it a very powerful plugin system. You can benefit from "
"extra functionality and need not to wait until someone integrates it into "
"&quantaplus;! The plugins can be loaded into a number of &GUI; elements. "
"More on this below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Understanding the Edit Plugin Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To install a Plugin or KPart we will work from the <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Plugins</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Edit</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"menu. This will bring up the following dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Edit Plugin dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog lets you manage all defined plugins and lets you add new ones. "
"We will describe each &GUI; element in here:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search paths"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can fill in a search path. When adding a plugin without a "
"<guilabel>Location</guilabel>, &quantaplus; will search these paths to find "
"the plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Add</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will bring up a dialog which allows you to add a new plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure"
msgstr "Configurar"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will allow you to change the settings of a particular plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove"
msgstr "Suprimir"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes the currently selected plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "Refresh"
msgstr "Actualizar"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "Refreshes the dialog's contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Read <xref linkend=\"configure-plugins\"/> to learn more about plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid "Team Development"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Often a project has more than one people working on it and there is some "
"kind of hierarchical relationsship between them. &quantaplus; supports the "
"notion of team members and they are configurable in the <menuchoice> "
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Project Properties</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "The team member editor dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Name</guilabel>, <guilabel>Email</guilabel> entries are self "
"explaining. <guilabel>Nickname</guilabel> is the nick of the user and acts "
"as an unique identifier."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Role</guilabel> specifies the role of the member in the project "
"and can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "Team leader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Subproject Leader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "Task Leader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple Member"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Task</guilabel> is a description of the task assigned to this "
"member."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Subproject</guilabel>: you can select a list of subproject. "
"Subprojects can be configured and created by pressing the <guilabel>Edit "
"subprojects</guilabel> button. Each subproject has a user visible name and a "
"location entry, the later specifying a relative path to a directory under "
"the project tree. This means that a subproject is a directory under the main "
"project. For example the main project can be the website of your company, "
"while a subproject can be the website for the intranet, located under the "
"<filename path=\"intranet\">intranet</filename> folder in the project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One member can have more than one role in the project, like both team leader "
"and subproject leader."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user should select who is himself from the list of the team members. "
"This is possible by selecting a team member from the list and pressing the "
"<guilabel>Set to Yourself</guilabel> button. The currently selected member "
"(your identity) appears in bold after the <guilabel>You are:</guilabel> text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Nicknames and setting yourself is important regarding messaging and "
"annotations. See <xref linkend=\"annotations\"/> to learn more about "
"annotations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Aside of keeping track of your team, there is one more benefit of setting up "
"the team members: you can configure an event to inform the team leaders when "
"some action happens. See <xref linkend=\"event-actions\"/> about how to do "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Event Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Event actions are actions executed when some event happens in the project. "
"An example would be logging when the project was opened and closed, so it "
"can be later reviewed how much one worked on it, or sending a mail when a "
"file is saved, or adding the file to the CVS with the help of a script when "
"the file is added to the project and the list could continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Event Configuration</guilabel> page of the <menuchoice> "
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Project Properties</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> dialog you can create, edit and delete the event "
"actions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "The event editor dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid "The entries in the dialog are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "Event"
msgstr "Eveniment"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the action is executed when the event selected from the list happens. The "
"event names are self explanatory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Action"
msgstr "Accion"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid "the type of the executed action. The possible choices are"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "Non-script action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"an action that is not a user defined script action. See <xref linkend=\"user-"
"actions\"/> for user action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:488 adv-quanta.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Action name</guilabel> specifies the action to be executed when "
"the event happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid "Send email"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"an email is sent when the action happens to the recipient selected in the "
"<guilabel>Receiver</guilabel> list. The recipient can be a team or "
"subproject leader. See <xref linkend=\"team-members\"/> for defining such "
"leaders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Log event"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "the event is logged in a file. The arguments for this action are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "Log file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "the filename with full path"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: adv-quanta.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detail"
msgstr "Detalhs"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "How much information will the log contain"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr "Compòrtament"

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether to create/overwrite the existing log file or append the new logged "
"event to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: adv-quanta.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid "Script action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"an user defined script action. See <xref linkend=\"user-actions\"/> for user "
"action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other entries depend on the <guilabel>Action</guilabel> type as they "
"were described."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid "Annotations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Annotations are special comments in the documents. They differ from regular "
"comments by the following things:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the information is collected by Quanta and shown in the "
"<guilabel>Annotations</guilabel> toolview."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "the information can be addressed to a team member"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entering annotations is simple. You can either use the <guilabel>Annotate</"
"guilabel> entry from the editor context menu or enter the "
"<emphasis>@annotation</emphasis> keyword in a comment area followed by the "
"annotation text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid "Annotation example in XML"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;!-- @annotation It is possible  that this code is wrong. --&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;!-- @annotation\n"
" Multiline \n"
" annotation. \n"
"--&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "Annotation example in PHP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"/* @annotation \n"
"Use PHP comments when annotating a PHP area\n"
"*/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Annotations can be addressed for a specific member of your team. The syntax "
"in this case is <emphasis>@annotation(nickname)</emphasis> or "
"<emphasis>@annotation(role)</emphasis>, where <emphasis>nickname</emphasis> "
"is the nickname of a team member, while <emphasis>role</emphasis> is a "
"project role from the following items: <itemizedlist> <listitem><para> team "
"leader </para></listitem> <listitem><para> task leader </para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para> subproject leader </para></listitem> </itemizedlist> The "
"task and subproject leaders should be followed by the corresponding task and "
"subproject name, like it is shown in the below examples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make a note to a team member with the nickname <emphasis>eric</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;-- @annotation(eric) Eric, please look at this. Andras --&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inform the team leader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;-- @annotation(team leader) This is very important for the team --&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: adv-quanta.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inform the <emphasis>PHP</emphasis> subproject leader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: adv-quanta.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "// @annotation(subproject leader:PHP) What do you think about it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Nicknames and role names are case insensitive, but spaces around brackets "
"and the <emphasis>:</emphasis> make the annotation invalid."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More about team members, roles and nicknames can be found in <xref linkend="
"\"team-members\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: adv-quanta.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The annotations found in the project can be inspected in the "
"<guilabel>Annotations</guilabel> view. It consists of tree tabs: "
"<variablelist> <varlistentry> <term><guilabel>Current File</guilabel></term> "
"<listitem><para> The annotation found in the current file.</para></listitem> "
